---
import DocsLayout from '../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
import LayerDiagram from '../components/LayerDiagram.astro';
import SourceBlock from '../components/SourceBlock.astro';
import { getCounts, getRegistry, version } from '../lib/harness/registry.ts';
import { honesty, listCli } from '../lib/harness/cli.ts';
import { REPO_URL } from '../lib/harness/paths.ts';

const c = getCounts();
const r = getRegistry();
const cli = listCli();
const h = honesty();
const v = version();

const install = [
  'git clone https://github.com/JakeSelby/agent-harness.git ~/repos/agent-harness',
  'cd ~/repos/agent-harness',
  'bin/harness install',
  '# Homebrew packages, VS Code + extensions, Claude Code, Codex, gh, then sync',
].join('\n');

const headings = [
  { depth: 2, slug: 'how-it-loads', text: 'How it loads' },
  { depth: 2, slug: 'what-you-get', text: 'What you get' },
  { depth: 2, slug: 'the-ritual', text: 'The ritual' },
  { depth: 2, slug: 'the-cli', text: 'The CLI' },
  { depth: 2, slug: 'honest', text: 'It keeps itself honest' },
];
---

<DocsLayout
  title="Overview"
  description="agent-harness: the rules, stances, skills, agents, commands, hooks and output style that make a Claude Code agent legible, predictable and reviewable. The reference, built from the checkout."
  crumbs={[{ label: 'overview', mono: true }]}
  sourcePath="README.md"
  sourceLabel="View README on GitHub"
  headings={headings}
  kind="Overview"
  wide
>
  <section class="block hero">
    <div class="eyebrow">
      <span class="pill">Open source</span><span class="pill">MIT</span><span class="pill">Python 3.9 stdlib</span><span class="pill">Claude Code · Codex · VS Code</span>
    </div>
    <h1>The harness that makes a coding agent legible, predictable and reviewable.</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      An installable set of rules, preference stances, skills, agents, commands, hooks and an output style for Claude Code.
      The git checkout <em>is</em> the live configuration, so every change to how the agent behaves is a commit.
    </p>
    <div class="cta">
      <a class="btn primary" href={REPO_URL}>
        <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M15 22v-4a4.8 4.8 0 0 0-1-3.5c3 0 6-2 6-5.5.08-1.25-.27-2.48-1-3.5.28-1.15.28-2.35 0-3.5 0 0-1 0-3 1.5-2.64-.5-5.36-.5-8 0C6 2 5 2 5 2c-.3 1.15-.3 2.35 0 3.5A5.403 5.403 0 0 0 4 9c0 3.5 3 5.5 6 5.5-.39.49-.68 1.05-.85 1.65-.17.6-.22 1.23-.15 1.85v4" /><path d="M9 18c-4.51 2-5-2-7-2" /></svg>
        View on GitHub
      </a>
      <a class="btn" href="/install/">Install and configure</a>
      <a class="btn" href="/skills/plan-authoring/">Read a skill page</a>
      <a class="btn" href="/stances/testing/">Compare a stance</a>
    </div>
    <div class="install">
      <SourceBlock code={install} lang="sh" label="Install in sixty seconds" />
    </div>
    <div class="pillars">
      <div>
        <span class="k">Legible</span>
        <h3>Read what it did without scrolling</h3>
        <p>Verdict first, registers separated, action items in one place. The <a href="/output-styles/scannable/">Scannable</a> output style shapes every reply.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <span class="k">Predictable</span>
        <h3>Delegates, verifies and asks the same way every time</h3>
        <p>{c.rules} short rules load every turn; skills carry the reasoning on demand; hooks enforce what a rule can only advise.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <span class="k">Reviewable</span>
        <h3>A plan fits on one screen</h3>
        <p>The <a href="/skills/plan-authoring/">Review Card</a> ends with numbered decisions you answer in chat. Nothing builds without an explicit go-ahead.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="block" id="how-it-loads">
    <h2>How it loads</h2>
    <p class="section-lede">
      Nine layers, in load order. Every arrow is a symlink made by <code>harness sync</code>; the one file that is merged rather than linked is
      <code>settings.json</code>, because Claude Code writes to it too.
    </p>
    <LayerDiagram />
    <p class="ladder-note">
      Your own <code>~/.claude/rules/*.md</code> sit alongside, untouched. <code>harness sync</code> never replaces a file it did not create;
      <code>harness uninstall</code> puts everything back. The whole story is in <a href="/docs/how-it-works/">How it works</a>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="block" id="what-you-get">
    <h2>What you get</h2>
    <div class="counts">
      <a href="/rules/"><span class="n num">{c.rules}</span><span class="lbl">Rules</span></a>
      <a href="/stances/"><span class="n num">{c.stanceDimensions}<small>· {c.stanceVariants} variants</small></span><span class="lbl">Stances</span></a>
      <a href="/skills/"><span class="n num">{c.skills}</span><span class="lbl">Skills</span></a>
      <a href="/agents/"><span class="n num">{c.agents}</span><span class="lbl">Agents</span></a>
      <a href="/commands/"><span class="n num">{c.commands}</span><span class="lbl">Commands</span></a>
      <a href="/hooks/"><span class="n num">{c.hooks}</span><span class="lbl">Hooks</span></a>
      <a href="/output-styles/"><span class="n num">{c.outputStyles}</span><span class="lbl">Output style</span></a>
      <a href="/docs/"><span class="n num">{c.docs}</span><span class="lbl">Docs</span></a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="block" id="the-ritual">
    <h2>The ritual, in {c.commands} keystrokes</h2>
    <div class="ritual">
      {r.commands.map((cmd, i) => (
        <>
          <a href={cmd.route}>{cmd.label}</a>
          {i < r.commands.length - 1 && <span class="arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span>}
        </>
      ))}
    </div>
    <p class="ritual-note">
      Read-only gatherers fan out for one digest; a Review Card stops at the build gate; the build lands in its own worktree and opens the pull request;
      two fresh contexts review scope then quality; the handoff file is what the next session reads.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="block" id="the-cli">
    <h2>The CLI</h2>
    <dl class="cli">
      {cli.map((cmd) => (
        <>
          <dt><a href={`/cli/#${cmd.name}`}>{cmd.name}</a></dt>
          <dd>{cmd.help}</dd>
        </>
      ))}
    </dl>
  </section>

  <section class="block" id="honest">
    <h2>It keeps itself honest</h2>
    <div class="honest">
      <div>
        <b>{h.cap} lines, always loaded, lint-enforced</b>
        <code>CLAUDE.md</code> plus the rules plus the longest variant of every stance may never exceed the cap. <code>harness lint</code> fails the commit if they do.
      </div>
      <div>
        <b class="num">{h.tests} tests on every push</b>
        The CLI, the hooks and the lint are covered by {h.testFiles} standard-library test files; CI runs lint then tests on every push and pull request.
      </div>
      <div>
        <b>The checkout is the configuration</b>
        Symlinks, not copies. Edit the file, commit, and the change is live in the next session; <code>harness diff</code> shows anything that drifted.
      </div>
      <div>
        <b>Nothing personal in the tree</b>
        Identity, stances and permissions live in <code>~/.config/agent-harness/config.json</code>; the lint scans every tracked file for personal-data shapes and secrets.
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="ritual-note">This page is generated from the <code>v{v}</code> tag of the repository. Every count, description and CLI line above is read from the checkout at build time.</p>
  </section>
</DocsLayout>
